## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-10, honoring R16 and D7 (both notes and annotations). Verified
gap at edf2748: builds crawl top:true only — standalone notes are indexed,
child notes and annotations are not, so the researcher's own words are
invisible while zoteus can create annotations it can never find again. The PR:
an itemType-filtered second crawl pass for child notes + annotations, #6012
eligibility cited (they embed both as first-class).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] child notes and annotations indexed; failing test shows today's blindness
- [ ] record-core ruling respected: own words extend, never dilute — via source label widening (`source: 'note'|'annotation'`); per-field columns stay RFC-scope
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
Scope correction: "own field/column" cannot mean an FTS column upstream — the
schema has one text column. It means a source: 'note'|'annotation' label
extending the existing source: 'fulltext' pattern (backend.ts:38 widens). The
crawl pattern to copy is fulltext-source.ts:87-92 (itemType: 'attachment');
the local client passes itemType through (local-client.ts:99-101).
